      "raw_response": "REFUTED\n\nThe abstract does not support the claim that allogeneic mechanical circulatory support is not as effective as autologous mechanical circulatory support for treating acute myocardial infarction. In fact, the study found that both allogeneic and autologous MSC therapies were associated with low rates of treatment-emergent SAEs and improved patient functional capacity, quality of life, and ventricular remodeling. The study also found that low-dose concentration MSCs (20 million cells) produced greatest reductions in LV volumes and increased EF, which suggests that allogeneic MSC therapy may be as effective as autologous MSC therapy in certain aspects.",
